Doom on FreePascalOS
====================

doom is the doomgeneric engine in a window of the display server. It
needs an IWAD, the game's data, and looks for one in, in this order:

  1. the current folder
  2. the folder (or the file) named by DOOMWADDIR
  3. the folders of DOOMWADPATH (separated by colons)
  4. /usr/local/share/games/doom
  5. /usr/share/games/doom

The freedoom package installs Freedoom (free game data, BSD licence) in
/usr/local/share/games/doom:

  doom                         Freedoom: Phase 1 (Doom's episodes)
  doom -iwad freedoom2.wad     Freedoom: Phase 2 (Doom II's levels)

Your own WADs: copy an IWAD you own (doom.wad, doom2.wad, plutonia.wad,
tnt.wad, or the shareware doom1.wad) into /usr/local/share/games/doom,
or anywhere with DOOMWADDIR pointing there; doom then starts it rather
than Freedoom (doom -iwad freedoom1.wad still picks Freedoom). Add-on
levels load with doom -file NAME.wad.

Settings and saved games go to ~/.doom/ (default.cfg, and
savegame/IWAD/ for each game's saves).

Keys: arrows move and turn, Ctrl fires, Space opens doors and presses
switches, Shift runs, Alt strafes (with the arrows), 1-7 choose weapons,
Tab shows the map, Escape opens the menu, Enter and Y/N answer it, F2
saves, F3 loads, F11 changes the gamma. Closing the window quits.

Sound effects play through /dev/audio when the system has an audio
output; music is not played yet.
